{title: 620 - On Jordan's Stormy Banks}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]On Jordan’s stormy [Fm]banks I [Bb7]stand,
[Eb]And cast a [Cm]wish[Eb]ful [Fm7]eye [Bb]
[G7]To [Cm]Canaan’s [Gm]fair [Ab]and [Eb]happy [Ab2]land,
[Fm7]Where [Eb]my [Gm]pos[Fm]ses[Bb7]sions [Eb]lie.
[Eb]I am bound [Ebmaj7]for the [Ab]prom[Eb]ised [Ab]land,
[Bb]I am [Eb]bound [Ebmaj7]for the [Cm]prom[Gm]ised [Fm]lan[Bb]d;
[G]O [Cm]who will [Gm]come [Ab]and [Eb]go with [Ab2]me?
[Fm7]I am [Eb]bound [Gm]for the [Fm]prom[Bb7]ised [Eb]land.

Refrain:
[Eb]I am [Fm]bound for [Bb7]the promised land,
[Eb]I [Cm]am [Eb]bound for [Fm7]the [Bb]promised land;
[G7]O [Cm]who [Gm]will come [Ab]and [Eb]go [Ab2]with me?
[Fm7]I [Eb]am [Gm]bound [Fm]for [Bb7]the [Eb]promised land.

Verse 2:
[Eb]O'er all [Fm]those wide [Bb7]extended plain
[Eb][Cm]Shines [Eb]one [Fm7]eternal [Bb]day;
[G7]There, [Cm]Christ, [Gm]the [Ab]Sun, [Eb]for [Ab2]ever reigns,
[Fm7][Eb]And [Gm]scatters [Fm][Bb7]night [Eb]away.

Verse 3:
[Eb]When shall [Fm]I reach [Bb7]that happy place,
[Eb][Cm]And [Eb]be [Fm7]forever [Bb]blest?
[G7]When [Cm]shall [Gm]I [Ab]see [Eb]my [Ab2]Father's face,
[Fm7][Eb]And [Gm]in [Fm]His [Bb7]kingdom [Eb]rest?

Verse 4:
[Eb]Filled with [Fm]delight, my [Bb7]raptured soul
[Eb]Would [Cm]here [Eb]no [Fm7]longer [Bb]stay;
[G7]Though [Cm]Jordan's [Gm]waves [Ab]around [Eb]me [Ab2]roll,
[Fm7][Eb]Fearless [Gm]I'd [Fm][Bb7]launch [Eb]away.
